1. Problem Statement (Scenario)
We want to simulate:

👉 “What happens to EMI when Interest Rate changes?”
👉 “What happens to Profit when Cost/Price changes?”

This is called What-if Analysis in Power BI.

🔷 2. Sample Dataset (Loan Data)

Create an Excel table like this:

Customer	Loan Amount	Tenure 
A	500000	5
B	800000	10
C	300000	3
D	1000000	15

👉 Load this into Power BI:

Open Power BI

Click Home → Get Data → Excel → Load

🔷 3. Create What-if Parameter (Interest Rate)
Step:

Go to Modeling Tab

Click New Parameter

Configure:

Name: Interest Rate

Data Type: Decimal Number

Min: 5

Max: 15

Increment: 0.5

Default: 8

✅ This creates:

Parameter table

Slicer (auto)

🔷 4. EMI Formula (Core Logic)

EMI Formula:

Where:

P = Loan Amount

r = Monthly Interest Rate

n = Number of Months

🔷 5. Create Measure for EMI

Go to Modeling → New Measure

EMI = 
VAR LoanAmount = SUM('LoanData'[Loan Amount])
VAR AnnualRate = SELECTEDVALUE('Interest Rate'[Interest Rate Value])
VAR MonthlyRate = AnnualRate / 12 / 100
VAR TenureMonths = SUM('LoanData'[Tenure (Years)]) * 12

RETURN 
(LoanAmount * MonthlyRate * POWER(1 + MonthlyRate, TenureMonths)) /
(POWER(1 + MonthlyRate, TenureMonths) - 1)
